# Project Memory (forced)

ALWAYS apply. No opt-out. One memory system only: `.cursor/memory/` at the workspace root.

## Create if missing

If `.cursor/memory/` does not exist:

1. Create `.cursor/memory/` and `.cursor/memory/research/`.
2. Seed `project.md`, `activeContext.md`, `progress.md`, `decisions.md` (use light-controller templates if available under `~/Projects/cursor-master-controller-light/templates/memory/`).
3. If workspace root has no `AGENTS.md`, copy the light-controller `templates/AGENTS.md`.

## Before non-trivial work

Read at least:

- `.cursor/memory/project.md`
- `.cursor/memory/activeContext.md`
- `.cursor/memory/progress.md`

Also Read task-matched files under `.cursor/memory/research/` only. Do not dump the entire tree when large.

## During work

When you discover durable project knowledge (stack, commands, architecture, decisions, constraints), save it immediately to the appropriate file.

## After significant progress

1. Update `activeContext.md` (overwrite OK for current focus).
2. Append a dated block to `progress.md`.
3. Append dated decisions to `decisions.md` when a choice was made.

## End of task

Memory pass required. If nothing durable changed, append one dated line to `progress.md`: `no durable updates`.

## Hard bans

- Never store secrets, tokens, API keys, `.env` contents, or credentials.
- Do not create parallel Memory Bank mode folders or a separate `context/` memory tree.
- Append history in `progress.md` / `decisions.md`; do not erase prior dated entries.
